From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:36:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/59] PCI: rockchip: dw: defined Wi-Fi power state when
 rfkill-wlan cannot answer

rk_pcie_establish_link() and rockchip_dw_pcie_suspend() declare "power"
uninitialised and ignore the return of rfkill_get_wifi_power_state().
The function returns -1 without writing *power while rfkill-wlan has
not probed, and the !IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_RFKILL_RK) stub (RFKILL_RK=m
with a built-in host driver) does the same. Each bcmdhd RESET then
picks a branch from stack contents: skip L2, or hold PERST low.

Start from power = 1 and use the value only when the call succeeds, so
an unknown state takes the powered path (L2 handshake, normal PERST
timing), the path 6.1 takes on success. 6.12 t6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
index a80098fc9..9d7d67e00 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
@@ -550,7 +550,7 @@ static bool rk_pcie_check_keep_power_in_suspend(struct rk_pcie *rk_pcie)
 
 static int rk_pcie_establish_link(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 {
-	int retries, power;
+	int retries, power = 1;
 	struct rk_pcie *rk_pcie = to_rk_pcie(pci);
 	int hw_retries = 0;
 	u32 ltssm;
@@ -594,8 +594,7 @@ static int rk_pcie_establish_link(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 		 * work fine. If it doesn't, please add more in DT node by add rockchip,perst-inactive-ms.
 		 */
 		if (rk_pcie->in_suspend && rk_pcie->skip_scan_in_resume) {
-			rfkill_get_wifi_power_state(&power);
-			if (!power) {
+			if (!rfkill_get_wifi_power_state(&power) && !power) {
 				gpiod_set_value_cansleep(rk_pcie->rst_gpio, 1);
 				return 0;
 			}
@@ -2214,7 +2213,7 @@ static void rk_pcie_downstream_dev_to_d0(struct rk_pcie *rk_pcie, bool enable)
 static int __maybe_unused rockchip_dw_pcie_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct rk_pcie *rk_pcie = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-	int ret = 0, power;
+	int ret = 0, power = 1;
 	struct dw_pcie *pci = rk_pcie->pci;
 	u32 status;
 
@@ -2248,8 +2247,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused rockchip_dw_pcie_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	 * must fail. Skip L2 routine.
 	 */
 	if (rk_pcie->skip_scan_in_resume) {
-		rfkill_get_wifi_power_state(&power);
-		if (!power)
+		if (!rfkill_get_wifi_power_state(&power) && !power)
 			goto no_l2;
 	}
 
